        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Prof. Robinson has been my favorite professor so far. She wants you to do well in her class and really cares for her students (cancelled lecture one day for mental health and bought donuts). The class is basically all writing, so be prepared for that. As long as you can write in Spanish well enough, you should do well in the class. Would recommend!",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Emma is a great person overall and probably my favorite professor. She's really caring to you and is very easy to talk to. She's very sweet and is really one of the few reasons why this semester had an upside to it. If you have the chance to have her for a class, she is a no-brainer, take her class!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Emma is super understanding and flexible. The class has a relatively low courseload and she gives you detailed feedback to help you succeed. I would definitely recommend taking a Spanish class with her.",
                "difficulty_rating": 1,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "She was one of my all time favorite professors, and she's was only a grad student. She made the course challenging, but was there to answer questions each step of the way. She responds quickly to emails and is very approachable when you don't understand. Do all of the homework with a reasonable amount of studying, and SPAN 203 is any easy A.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            }
